    "turn_idx": 62,
    "turn_text": "The Democrats have a lot of soul searching to do to figure out why with all their hard work. I can't tell how many people I know in my life that were in Pennsylvania knocking on doors. I, you know, I, this is, this is my personal thing, right? James Carvel said it's the economy stupid. Biden never rose much above 40% for the last few years in terms of his overall approval rating. It's really hard to overcome to, to re up as the president. It just historically is. Forget about personalities. It just is. It was Ronald Reagan who famously asked, are you better off now four years ago or now? It's a tough question for people. Grocery bills are really high. They're really high, congressmen, which had to be with Congressman Jim Himes. Is that all Biden's fault? Probably not, probably not. But you end up having to take the blame and the credit for your four years, whatever it is. I don't know. They're going to write a lot of history books about this. And then you know what? The moments in this campaign that stood out. I mean, Donald Trump took a bullet and he came in that moment with that fist. Come on, Congressman. That was pretty unbelievable. Whether you",
